{
 "version": 1,
 "name": "OSPF on a point-to-point triangle",
 "about": "R1-R2-R3 in a ring of point-to-point links. R1-R2 and R2-R3 cost 10 each, the direct R1-R3 link costs 50 from R1 and 60 from R3 (no equal-cost ties: the engine does not model ECMP forwarding), so R1 reaches H3's LAN through R2 (cost 20+10). Hello 1 s, dead 4 s. R1's cable to R2 is cut (R1 then takes the direct link) and restored.",
